  <section id="scoreboard">
    <p class="eyebrow">Scoreboard</p>
    <h2>Fast read on the tradeoffs</h2>
    <div class="rubric-note"><b>How these scores work:</b> Budget is weighted <b>double</b> against your $12k target / $15k strongly preferred maximum; Weather, Swim, Variety, Ease, Food, Risk, <b>Nights</b>, and <b>Novelty</b> are each rated 1-5 once. Total is out of 50 (PTO is tracked as data but not part of the default total). <b>Nights</b> rewards trip length: 12+ nights &rarr; 5, 11 &rarr; 4, 10 &rarr; 3, 9 &rarr; 2, 8 or fewer &rarr; 1 &mdash; more vacation for the same overhead. <b>Novelty</b> scores route overlap against the places already visited (California, Maui, Polignano a Mare, Monopoli, Alberobello, Matera, Ostuni, Locorotondo, Bari, Split, Dubrovnik, Hvar, Santorini, Mykonos, Rhodes, Positano, Capri, Naples): 5 = genuinely new, 1 = mostly repeats. Card order follows this table; default ties prefer a range within the budget preference, then fewer PTO days, then lower budget ceiling and floor. Cost never removes an itinerary. One explicit exception: <b>Croatia is excluded by family decision (2026 repeat)</b> &mdash; its score stays visible, but it sits unranked at the bottom. Date labels use valid 2027 windows.</div>
    <div class="score-legend"><span class="good"><i></i>Green = preferred / strong</span><span class="mixed"><i></i>Amber = workable tradeoff</span><span class="weak"><i></i>Rust = weak fit</span></div>
