      <article class="winner-card"><h3>Epic scenery + hiking</h3><p><b>Madeira + Mallorca</b> &mdash; the same Arieiro-above-the-clouds, 25 Fontes, Porto Moniz week, paired with a Mediterranean swim that keeps the whole trip under the $15k preferred maximum. <b>Madeira + Crete</b> and <b>Madeira + Sicily</b> offer the same hiking but both now cross the preferred maximum.</p></article>
      <article class="winner-card"><h3>Pure score</h3><p><b>Portugal</b> at 41/50, then <b>Madeira + Mallorca</b> at 39 and <b>Portugal + Sicily</b> at 37. <b>Hawaii</b> is #12 at 32/50: its $11k&ndash;15.8k range crosses the preferred maximum and it delivers only nine hotel nights.</p></article>
      <article class="winner-card"><h3>Best Italy route</h3><p><b>Italy: Salento-Amalfi</b> because it has the best food/variety stretch, even after the budget drift made it a preference-fit trim decision.</p></article>
      <article class="winner-card"><h3>Warm-water Europe</h3><p><b>Turkish Riviera</b> has the warmest non-Hawaii sea on the board (75&ndash;79&deg;F) and a clean three-base AYT-to-DLM route. It ranks #11 at 33/50 because heat, long-haul airfare, the scoped advisory, and a ~$17.4k high case offset the swim advantage.</p></article>
      <article class="winner-card"><h3>Best Europe value</h3><p><b>Croatia</b> wins value on paper ($8.6k&ndash;12.8k) but is excluded &mdash; 2026 repeat, novelty 1/5. <b>Greece via Lisbon</b> ($9.9k&ndash;15.6k) has the next-lowest floor, though its ceiling now also crosses the preferred maximum.</p></article>
