  <section id="risks">
    <p class="eyebrow">Plan Health-Check</p>
    <h2>Risks worth keeping visible</h2>
    <ul class="hc-list">
      <li class="fixed"><strong>The bias is retired.</strong> The Portugal/Italy preference no longer touches the ranking &mdash; under the old order it was worth up to ten rank positions (Madeira + Sicily sat #5 despite the board's worst risk score). Hearts still say Portugal/Italy; the data says <b>Portugal</b> first at 41, Madeira + Mallorca second at 39, Portugal + Sicily third at 37, and Iceland fourth at 36 &mdash; all still June-Med swim 3, since genuine warm water only shows up at Turkey's sea and Hawaii.</li>
      <li class="solid"><strong>Hybrids resolve the core tension.</strong> All five hybrids keep a Portugal opener and hand the swimming to warm water elsewhere. Madeira openers buy epic hiking at the cost of extra flight legs and FNC wind risk; mainland openers stay calm and cheap. Crete and Sicily legs feed the Italy/Greece bias but press the preferred maximum; the newest hybrid, Madeira + Mallorca, is the only one that keeps the Madeira hiking week and stays within-preference.</li>
      <li class="head"><strong>Madeira runs on gates and buffers.</strong> Every Madeira variant only works as designed: one protected ticket, the Lisbon buffer night before the onward hop (FNC wind delays peak in summer), and a hard family-airfare gate. The Sicily variants also ride a thinned-out air map: Ryanair exited Lisbon&ndash;Palermo in Nov 2024, leaving an easyJet monopoly with no low-cost floor &mdash; though Catania does carry a seasonal Delta JFK nonstop (Apr&ndash;Oct), so the fragile leg is the Lisbon&ndash;Palermo fare, not the US connection.</li>
      <li class="act"><strong>Italy drifted expensive.</strong> The Salento-Maratea-Amalfi file now reads ~$13.2k-16.4k realistic, with a preference-fit trim around ~$12.4k-14.8k. It is a stretch finalist, not a budget-safe pick.</li>
      <li class="act"><strong>Hawaii's own rollup crosses the preferred maximum.</strong> The scoreboard used to say $10.6k&ndash;14.4k; Hawaii's line-item budget table sums to ~$11k&ndash;15.8k with insurance. Combined with only 9 hotel nights and a been-there Maui factor, it now sits #12 even before quotes land.</li>
      <li class="head"><strong>Turkey is a warm-water wild card, not the automatic winner.</strong> The Turkish Riviera has the warmest non-Hawaii sea on the board, but June heat, long-haul airfare, the scoped advisory, and a reconciled high case near $17.4k hold it to #11 at 33/50.</li>
      <li class="fixed"><strong>Croatia is excluded outright.</strong> Croatia scores 35/50 at the best warm-water price, but the family did Croatia in 2026 and this route repeats Split/Hvar/Korčula. Excluded from the recommendation by explicit decision; the row stays on the scoreboard for reference.</li>
      <li class="act"><strong>The Pittsburgh commitment drives the date math.</strong> Returning on Jun 23 is valid and preferred; every plan must keep the family in Pittsburgh for the full days Jun 24-26. Some plans still use Jun 9-22 for schedule or price reasons, while Balkans and California move into early July.</li>
      <li class="head"><strong>Complexity still matters.</strong> Sardinia/Corsica, Sicily/Malta, Greece via Lisbon, and the Balkans all offer major variety, but each adds either ferry, cross-border, flight-chain, or four-base friction. Balkans also picked up July peak-pricing risk.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="considered">
    <p class="eyebrow">Options Considered</p>
    <h2>The "Madeira-variety" exploration &mdash; combos we weighed</h2>
    <details class="considered-box">
      <summary>Every epic-hiking / swim-variety combo we discussed, and why most weren't built</summary>
      <p class="considered-intro">Sparked by Madeira's mid-trip flight friction plus wanting a leg with epic hiking and dramatically different scenery <em>and</em> good swimming &mdash; while staying novel against the Mediterranean-beach board and our recent Mexico trip. Captured here so we don't lose the thread.</p>

      <h3 class="considered-h">Built / in progress</h3>
      <ul class="considered-list">
        <li><strong>Canary Islands</strong> (Tenerife + La Palma) &mdash; <span class="st st-go">built, ranked #16 (31/50)</span> Madeira's ecological twin (Macaronesian laurel forest + Teide volcano) &mdash; but flight connectivity is the tradeoff, not the upgrade: Pittsburgh to Tenerife/La Palma typically runs three connections via Madrid, versus Madeira's single-stop United EWR&ndash;FNC nonstop.</li>
        <li><strong>Albania</strong> (Accursed Mountains: Theth/Valbona + the Riviera: Ksamil) &mdash; <span class="st st-go">built, scores highest (44/50), excluded by family decision</span> The best <em>warm-sea + novel</em> pick: alpine drama + Caribbean-clear swimming, cheap, one-country ground transport, no island-hop trap.</li>
        <li><strong>Madeira + Mallorca</strong> &mdash; <span class="st st-go">built, top hybrid #2 (39/50)</span> The Madeira ridge-hiking week paired with a sandy Mediterranean swim in Mallorca instead of a second Atlantic or Greek leg &mdash; the only Madeira hybrid whose audited high case stays within the preferred maximum.</li>
        <li><strong>Dolomites + Venice + Sardinia</strong> &mdash; <span class="st st-go">built, ranked #9 (34/50)</span> Best pure epic-hiking (Tre Cime, Seceda) with a Venice opener and an epic-beach Sardinia finale. Landlocked hiking half = the variety.</li>
        <li><strong>Iceland</strong> (Reykjavík + Golden Circle + South Coast + Jökuls&aacute;rl&oacute;n) &mdash; <span class="st st-go">built, #4 on the data (36/50)</span> The most novel-looking option &mdash; nothing like the Med board or Mexico. Swim = warm geothermal lagoons, not the (cold) sea.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="considered-h">Prompts drafted, not yet built</h3>
      <ul class="considered-list">
        <li><strong>Crete &mdash; add epic hiking</strong> (Samaria Gorge, Imbros, Lefka Ori) &mdash; <span class="st st-draft">prompt ready</span> Not a new trip &mdash; an enhancement to the existing Crete legs so Crete alone carries the Madeira mountain-vs-sea variety with zero Atlantic flight.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="considered-h">Considered, set aside</h3>
      <ul class="considered-list">
        <li><strong>Costa Rica</strong> (Arenal + Monteverde + Manuel Antonio) &mdash; <span class="st st-no">off the table</span> A complete plan already existed, but it photographs like Yucat&aacute;n/Riviera Maya &mdash; no novelty right after a Mexico trip. The look is structural (beach + jungle), so a rebuild wouldn't fix it.</li>
        <li><strong>Slovenia</strong> (Julian Alps + So&ccaron;a + Bled) &mdash; <span class="st st-no">not built</span> Genuinely novel emerald-alpine look and cheap, but the swim is turquoise river/glacial lakes, not warm sea.</li>
        <li><strong>Swiss Bernese Oberland</strong> (Lauterbrunnen + glacial lakes) &mdash; <span class="st st-no">not built</span> Epic and unique, but pushes hard past the $15k preferred maximum &mdash; the likely budget-breaker.</li>
        <li><strong>Greek mainland</strong> (Zagori/Vikos + Pelion) &mdash; <span class="st st-no">not built</span> Deepest-gorge + stone-village hiking is novel, but it's still Greece (we have Crete) and the Aegean beaches read Med.</li>
        <li><strong>Montenegro</strong> (Durmitor + Bay of Kotor) &mdash; <span class="st st-no">not built</span> Epic canyon + warm sea, but likely overlaps the existing Balkans road-trip and the coast looks Med.</li>
        <li><strong>Azores</strong> &mdash; <span class="st st-no">rejected</span> Same via-Lisbon Atlantic bottleneck as Madeira &mdash; doesn't fix the connectivity problem that started all this.</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="considered-note">Also noted along the way: <strong>Corsica</strong> (already on the board inside Sardinia + Corsica) and <strong>Crete</strong> are the closest "Madeira mountain-vs-sea substitute you may already own." The recurring tension: Albania took the best warm-sea-and-novel slot, so what's left trades warm ocean (Iceland/Slovenia/Switzerland = lagoon/river/lake swim) or partly echoes the Med board (Greece/Montenegro).</p>
    </details>
  </section>
